{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_development", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "claim": "The device failed to detect a clinically significant ventricular tachycardia episode, violating reliability requirements under EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1.", "support_note": "Log confirms missed detection event.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "claim": "No patient harm occurred, but the risk remains serious due to potential recurrence or evolution of the arrhythmia.", "support_note": "Retrospective review confirms single self-resolving episode with no adverse outcome.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-art83-pms-system", "claim": "The incident requires investigation under post-market surveillance obligations per EU MDR Article 83.", "support_note": "Article mandates systematic gathering and analysis of safety data to determine corrective actions.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A", "claim": "The static-analysis reports do not provide relevant evidence for this specific incident.", "support_note": "Report explicitly states it is unrelated to the firmware module involved in this event.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2018A", "claim": "The static-analysis reports do not provide relevant evidence for this specific incident.", "support_note": "Report explicitly states it is unrelated to the firmware module involved in this event.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.72, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident involves a safety-critical failure where the device failed to flag a clinically significant ventricular tachycardia episode (VT), which is consistent with EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1 requirements for reliability and performance in electronic programmable systems. While no adverse outcome occurred, this represents a serious potential patient-safety risk due to missed detection of arrhythmia that could have led to cardiac arrest if the event had evolved differently or been repeated. The containment status is partial: while clinical exposure was limited to one self-resolving episode and no harm realized, the failure mode indicates a regression in safety-critical functionality (confidence-score logic) rather than being blocked by an automatic control before patient use.\n\nEvidence supports that this is not merely a nuisance alert or contained technical glitch; it involves a missed detection event confirmed by retrospective review. However, evidence supporting immediate field action (Severity 4/FSCA) is insufficient as there has been no recurrence and the single episode self-resolved without harm. Therefore, CAPA_INVESTIGATE is appropriate to determine root cause and prevent future occurrences.\n\nConfidence is moderate-high based on consistent logs but remains below 0.85 due to lack of historical data showing prior similar failures or explicit validation test results for this specific regression scenario in the retrieved artifacts.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "4632ed48df7d3ede87ed3df53ee1bc32ab4db720d117e1e19ff2265d8338c329", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0025", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0025_r5", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0025", "s